================================================================================
3. ONE TEST READ CLOSELY: tests/test_font_ref.py
================================================================================

The log's only cited path is `tests/test_font_ref.py`, used to support "95
printable ASCII glyphs ... validated against independent font fixtures".

  Left-hand side: `.freebuff/ref/font8x8_basic.h`, a vendored copy of
      dhepper/font8x8 (public domain), tracked in git:
        $ git ls-files | grep font8x8
        .freebuff/ref/font8x8_basic.h
      It is parsed by a regex over `{ 0x.., ... } , // U+XXXX` entries.
  Right-hand side: `kernel/src/font/font_data.rs`, the table the kernel embeds,
      parsed by a different regex (`FIRST_CHAR`, `LAST_CHAR`,
      `GLYPHS: [u8; GLYPH_COUNT * 8]`).

  Where each came from: the reference is a third-party font file that predates
  this repository; the right-hand side is generated from it by tools/gen-font.py.
  So the test is a fidelity check of the transform plus a byte-rot alarm, not a
  design check of the glyph shapes. That is the right oracle for "the embedded
  atlas matches the reference", and both sides are files on disk, not values the
  test computed from one another. The test is not circular.

  Counts, checked against the data rather than the prose:

    $ python tests/test_font_ref.py
    font: 95 glyphs (U+0020..U+007E) match reference byte-for-byte
    EXIT=0
    $ python - <<'EOF'
    import re
    t=open('kernel/src/font/font_data.rs',encoding='utf-8').read()
    first=int(re.search(r"FIRST_CHAR:\s*u8\s*=\s*(0x[0-9A-Fa-f]+)",t).group(1),16)
    last=int(re.search(r"LAST_CHAR:\s*u8\s*=\s*(0x[0-9A-Fa-f]+)",t).group(1),16)
    print("FIRST_CHAR", first, "LAST_CHAR", last, "count", last-first+1)
    EOF
    FIRST_CHAR 32 LAST_CHAR 126 count 95

  U+0020..U+007E is 95 code points (126-32+1), and the table has 95 entries.
  The log's "95" matches both the range and the data. It is wired into CI:
  scripts/check.sh:75 runs it.

